WEBVTT

00:00:00.860 --> 00:00:04.369
AI Moderator supports live academic discussions.

00:00:04.498 --> 00:00:09.473
Administrators define how the moderator
supports learning across activities.

00:00:09.547 --> 00:00:14.477
Start in People, where you create
teacher accounts and organise access.

00:00:14.551 --> 00:00:17.684
Next, prepare shared moderation profiles.

00:00:17.814 --> 00:00:21.412
Give each profile a clear purpose,
such as comparing evidence

00:00:21.452 --> 00:00:24.301
or exploring contrasting perspectives.

00:00:24.375 --> 00:00:29.123
Set the learning objective, discussion
rules and conversation language.

00:00:29.197 --> 00:00:34.227
Choose whether automatic moderation publishes
contributions, records decisions for

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.991
observation, or is switched off.

00:00:37.066 --> 00:00:40.562
Participation and timing
settings shape when support is

00:00:40.602 --> 00:00:43.633
considered, including planned pauses.

00:00:43.706 --> 00:00:48.636
Teachers then select a profile for
their dialogue and set up the activity.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:52.581
Together, administrators and
teachers determine how much, how and

00:00:52.621 --> 00:00:54.799
when the moderator participates.

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:58.460
Students develop and discuss their own ideas.
